{
  "slug": "js_date_methods_set",
  "course": "js",
  "order": 60,
  "url": "/js/js_date_methods_set.asp",
  "title": "JavaScript Set Date Methods",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JavaScript Set Date Methods"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Set Date methods let you set date values (years,\nmonths, days, hours, minutes, seconds, milliseconds) for a Date Object."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Set Date Methods"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Set Date methods are used for setting a part of a date:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Method", "Description"],
      "rows": [
        ["setDate()", "Set the day as a number (1-31)"],
        ["setFullYear()", "Set the year (yyyy)"],
        ["setHours()", "Set the hour (0-23)"],
        ["setMilliseconds()", "Set the milliseconds (0-999)"],
        ["setMinutes()", "Set the minutes (0-59)"],
        ["setMonth()", "Set the month (0-11)"],
        ["setSeconds()", "Set the seconds (0-59)"],
        ["setTime()", "Set the time (milliseconds since January 1, 1970)"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The setFullYear() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The setFullYear() method sets the year of a date object. In this example to 2020:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"January 01, 2025\");\n\nd.setFullYear(2020);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_setfullyear"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The setFullYear() method can optionally set month and day:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"January 01, 2025\");\n\nd.setFullYear(2020, 11, 3);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_setfullyear_options"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The setMonth() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The setMonth() method sets the month of a date object (0-11):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"January 01, 2025\");\n\nd.setMonth(11);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_setmonth"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The setDate() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The setDate() method sets the day of a date object (1-31):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"January 01, 2025\");\n\nd.setDate(15);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_setdate"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The setDate() method can also be used to add days to a date:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"January 01, 2025\");\n\nd.setDate(d.getDate() + 50);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_ahead"
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "If adding days shifts the month or year, the changes are handled automatically by the Date object."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The setHours() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The setHours() method sets the hours of a date object (0-23):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"January 01, 2025\");\n\nd.setHours(22);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_sethours"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The setHours() method can also be used to set minutes and\nseconds."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"January 01, 2025\");\n\nd.setHours(22, 10, 20);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_sethours2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The setMinutes() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The setMinutes() method sets the minutes of a date object (0-59):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"January 01, 2025\");\n\nd.setMinutes(30);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_setminutes"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The setSeconds() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The setSeconds() method sets the seconds of a date object (0-59):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"January 01, 2025\");\n\nd.setSeconds(30);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_setseconds"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Compare Dates"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Dates can easily be compared."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The following example compares today's date with January 14, 2100:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let text = \"\";\n\nconst today = new Date();\n\nconst someday = new Date();\n\n someday.setFullYear(2100, 0, 14);\n\nif (someday > today) {\n  text = \"Today is before January 14, 2100.\";\n} else {\n\n    text = \"Today is after January 14, 2100.\";\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_compare"
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "JavaScript counts months from 0 to 11. January is 0. December is 11."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Learn More:"
